========================================================================================
PURITY FORBIDS DIRECTIONAL COOLING
========================================================================================
  Post-sensing |1> branch is rho_p = (1-p)|psi_1><psi_1| + p I/d.
  p = 0 is the protocol as analysed in the manuscript.

  DEPOLARISING MIXING IS THE WRONG TEST, and it is worth recording why.
  rho_p = (1-p)|psi_1><psi_1| + p I/d has i[rho_p, H] = (1-p) i[|psi_1><psi_1|, H],
  because the identity commutes with H. Rank stays 2, everything scales, the
  interval stays exactly symmetric. Admixing the identity adds no asymmetry -
  which is the resource theory speaking: the maximally mixed state is FREE.
  The same argument kills the thermal state: [e^{-beta H}, H] = 0 exactly.

  A mixture must be of states that do NOT commute with H to raise rank(M11).

